      }
    ],
    "status": "present",
    "value": "Index colours 0..5 and store, for each ordered pair (l, r), a 6-bit mask of allowed tops. To test whether a row can reach the top, build the row above one cell at a time: cell i must be a colour in mask(row[i], row[i+1]). After choosing cell i (i > 0), prune immediately if the new pair (cell i-1, cell i) has no allowed top at all, because that row could never continue. When the next row is complete, recurse on it. Memoise the outcome per row, since many different paths produce the same row."
  },
